{"layout":"tutorial_hands_on","title":"Taxonomic Analysis of eDNA","zenodo_link":"https://zenodo.org/records/15367390","questions":["Can we assign taxonomic information to unknown DNA sequences from environmental samples?","What are the key bioinformatics techniques used in the taxonomic analysis of eDNA sequences?"],"objectives":["Upload raw sequencing data to the Galaxy platform.","Apply read trimming tools to improve the quality of eDNA sequence data.","Convert sequence data between FASTQ and FASTA formats.","Perform a BLASTN search against a nucleotide database to identify potential taxonomic matches.","Extract and interpret taxonomic information from the BLAST output table."],"time_estimation":"2H","key_points":["eDNA analysis provides a non-invasive method to gain insights into species presence and biodiversity without directly disturbing the organisms or their habitat.","While this tutorial focuses on eDNA, the fundamental workflow involving sequence quality control (trimming) and sequence identification (BLAST alignment) has broad applications in various biological research areas.","This tutorial demonstrates a basic workflow to extract potential genus and species names from BLAST output, providing a starting point for further taxonomic analysis."],"contributions":{"authorship":["jbeli11"],"reviewing":["shiltemann","jbeli11","yvanlebras"]},"tags":["biodiversity"],"subtopic":"ecologyanalysis","js_requirements":{"mathjax":5904,"mermaid":false},"short_id":"T00536","symlink":null,"url":"/topics/ecology/tutorials/eDNA-taxonomic-analysis/tutorial.html","topic_name":"ecology","tutorial_name":"eDNA-taxonomic-analysis","dir":"topics/ecology/tutorials/eDNA-taxonomic-analysis","id":"ecology/eDNA-taxonomic-analysis","hands_on":true,"slides":false,"mod_date":"2025-06-03 09:24:56 +0000","pub_date":"2025-06-02 10:39:17 +0000","version":2,"workflows":[{"workflow":"main_workflow.ga","tests":false,"url":"https://training.galaxyproject.org/training-material/topics/ecology/tuto